    "updated_at": "2024-07-19T17:23:29Z",
    "body": "That's not a border, it's a focus outline, indicating that the element has focus. Browsers are allowed some leeway in when they show a focus ring; in this case, I suspect that a button activation is considered \"obvious\" so it doesn't need an outline, but a non-button activation isn't, so they show one.\r\n\r\nIf you really want to suppress that, use the `outline` property.",
